  "worked_solution": "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $S$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QS}=\\overset{\\to }{QT}+\\overset{\\to }{TR}+\\overset{\\to }{RS}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/2297c60ae34a641e498aa41346778e327fd2286657914272088ddb9f9b03bcb7.png)\n\n  \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{TR}=c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{RS}=b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/fb4850a7d309448213c1ac5572dfe112555a2938790b24fad03ebb4669e3d95a.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QS} & =\\overset{\\to }{QT}+\\overset{\\to }{TR}+\\overset{\\to }{RS} \\\\  & =a+c+b.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
